Q: Explain DevOps in one minute.
 "DevOps is a culture and set of practices that bring development and operations teams together to automate and streamline the software delivery process. It focuses on Continuous Integration, Continuous Deployment, automation, monitoring, and collaboration. 
 The goal is to deliver high-quality software faster, reduce deployment failures, 
 improve system reliability, 
 and enhance customer satisfaction. 
 In modern IT environments, DevOps plays a critical role in achieving faster and more efficient software delivery.


Q. What are the technical and business benefits of the DevOps work culture?
Answer:
"Technically, DevOps provides faster deployments, better automation, improved reliability, faster recovery, and fewer manual errors. From a business perspective, it helps deliver features faster, reduces downtime and operational costs, and improves customer satisfaction."



